Z||000000||DISenchanted||01-31-2000||09:43 PM||||I have an 88gt with an auto trans, it shifts really late and I believe that it's because of the "detent" cable.  The cable that runs from the throttle body to the trans.  Does anyone know where I can aquire one?<P>Thanks,<P>DISenchanted<p>[This message has been edited by DISenchanted (edited 02-01-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||daved||01-31-2000||10:01 PM||||Well, I had the same problem when I bought my 86gt; the cable adjuster was broken, allowing the cable to be too long.<BR> I think the Fiero Store has them, but I came up with a quick fix that has worked fine for 5 months.  <BR>I took the brass innards out of a large "Marr" electrical connector. It just passes over the lead thingy on the end of the SS wire cable. you just pull it out a little on the SS wire (say about 1/2" in my case) and tighten down the screw!  Works a treat, but I will eventually buy a new cable to ensure the exact shift points.||||reg||1
